{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that repairs Java 11 code so that it correctly solves the given programming problem. The code reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Repair the following Java 11 code so that it correctly solves the programming problem. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your repaired code should implement the problem correctly, meaning that it should produce the correct output for any valid input.\nPrint your repaired code and also the confidence score you give to your repair. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<repaired_code>\n<your_repaired_code>\n</repaired_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the problem description:\n<problem_description>\nMr. Chanek has an integer represented by a string $$$s$$$. Zero or more digits have been erased and are denoted by the character _. There are also zero or more digits marked by the character X, meaning they're the same digit.Mr. Chanek wants to count the number of possible integer $$$s$$$, where $$$s$$$ is divisible by $$$25$$$. Of course, $$$s$$$ must not contain any leading zero. He can replace the character _ with any digit. He can also replace the character X with any digit, but it must be the same for every character X.As a note, a leading zero is any 0 digit that comes before the first nonzero digit in a number string in positional notation. For example, 0025 has two leading zeroes. An exception is the integer zero, (0 has no leading zero, but 0000 has three leading zeroes).\n</problem_description>\n\nHere is the Java 11 code you have to repair:\n<original_code>\nhttps://codeforces.com/problemset/submit/*\r\n25\r\nAny numbers that end in 00, 25, 50, or 75 will work - after can end in any groups of digits (can do casework on all possible endings) - just test if a certain starting group is possible - may also influence rest of string if one of the digits is an X\r\n*/\r\nimport java.util.*;\r\nimport java.io.*;\r\n\r\npublic class Main{\r\n  public static char[] str; \r\n  public static String[] ends = {\"00\", \"25\", \"50\", \"75\"};\r\n  public static long ret; \r\n  public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException{\r\n    BufferedReader br = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));\r\n\r\n    str = br.readLine().toCharArray(); \r\n    ret = 0; \r\n    if(str.length >= 2) for(int a = 0; a < 4; a++) match(str[str.length - 2], str[str.length - 1], ends[a]);\r\n    else{\r\n      if(str[0] == '0' || str[0] == 'X' || str[0] == '_') ret++; //only 0 possible, 0 divisible by 25\r\n    }\r\n\r\n    System.out.println(ret); \r\n      \r\n    br.close();\r\n  }\r\n  public static void match(char f, char s, String b){\r\n    //assume a is from the original string, b is the checking string \r\n    char f2 = f; \r\n    char s2 = s; \r\n    if(f == '_' && b.charAt(0) == '0' && str.length - 2 == 0) return; \r\n    if(f2 == 'X'){\r\n      //try to change f to the start of b\r\n      f2 = b.charAt(0);\r\n      if(s2 == 'X') s2 = b.charAt(0);\r\n    }\r\n    if(s2 == 'X'){\r\n      //try to change s to the end of b  \r\n      s2 = b.charAt(1);\r\n      if(f2 == 'X') f2 = b.charAt(1);\r\n    }\r\n    if(f2 == '_'){\r\n      //try to change f to the start of b\r\n      f2 = b.charAt(0);\r\n    }\r\n    if(s2 == '_'){\r\n      //try to change s to the end of b\r\n      s2 = b.charAt(1);\r\n    }\r\n    char cv = 'n'; //if f was X or s was X then xVal changes\r\n    if(f == 'X') cv = f2; \r\n    if(s == 'X') cv = s2;\r\n    //System.out.println(f2 + \" \" + s2 + \" \" + b);\r\n    if(f2 == b.charAt(0) && s2 == b.charAt(1)) poss(cv); \r\n  }\r\n  public static void poss(char xVal){\r\n    //xVal = -1 if xs not filled yet\r\n    //System.out.println(\"test \" + xVal);\r\n    if((xVal == '0' && str[0] == 'X') || str[0] == '0') return; //cannot start with a 0  \r\n    long add = 1; \r\n    boolean xF = false; //whether or not we set X\r\n    if(xVal != 'n') xF = true; \r\n    for(int a = 0; a < str.length - 2; a++){\r\n      if(str[a] == '_'){\r\n        if(a == 0) add *= 9; //1 2 3 4 5 6 7 8 9\r\n        else add *= 10; \r\n      }\r\n      if(!xF && str[a] == 'X'){\r\n        xF = true; \r\n        if(a == 0) add *= 9; \r\n        else add *= 10; \r\n      }\r\n    }\r\n    //System.out.println(\"add \" + add);\r\n    ret += add; \r\n  }\r\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<repaired_code>\nimport java.util.*;\nimport java.io.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static char[] str;\n    public static String[] validEndings = {\"00\", \"25\", \"50\", \"75\"};\n    public static long result;\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {\n        BufferedReader br = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));\n        str = br.readLine().toCharArray();\n        result = 0;\n\n        // Handle single digit case\n        if (str.length == 1) {\n            if (str[0] == '0' || str[0] == '_') {\n                result = 1; // only 0 is valid\n            } else if (str[0] == 'X') {\n                result = 1; // X can be 0\n            }\n            System.out.println(result);\n            br.close();\n            return;\n        }\n\n        // Try each valid ending for divisibility by 25\n        for (String ending : validEndings) {\n            if (isValidEnding(ending)) {\n                countValidNumbers(ending);\n            }\n        }\n\n        System.out.println(result);\n        br.close();\n    }\n\n    public static boolean isValidEnding(String ending) {\n        char first = str[str.length - 2];\n        char second = str[str.length - 1];\n        char expectedFirst = ending.charAt(0);\n        char expectedSecond = ending.charAt(1);\n\n        // Check if the ending is possible\n        if (first != '_' && first != 'X' && first != expectedFirst) return false;\n        if (second != '_' && second != 'X' && second != expectedSecond) return false;\n\n        // Handle X constraints\n        if (first == 'X' && second == 'X') {\n            // Both are X, they must be the same digit, but ending requires different digits for most cases\n            // Only \"00\" has same digits, so only valid for \"00\"\n            if (ending.equals(\"00\")) return true;\n            return false;\n        }\n\n        // Check if X constraints conflict with the ending\n        if (first == 'X') {\n            // All X must be same digit, so if second is also X, it must match\n            if (second == 'X') return ending.charAt(0) == ending.charAt(1);\n            // If second is fixed, X must match expectedFirst\n            return true;\n        }\n\n        if (second == 'X') {\n            // If first is fixed, X must match expectedSecond\n            return true;\n        }\n\n        return true;\n    }\n\n    public static void countValidNumbers(String ending) {\n        char firstEnd = ending.charAt(0);\n        char secondEnd = ending.charAt(1);\n\n        // Determine what digit X must be if present in the last two positions\n        char xDigit = 'n'; // 'n' means no X constraint from ending\n        if (str[str.length - 2] == 'X' || str[str.length - 1] == 'X') {\n            // If both are X, they must be same, so only valid for \"00\"\n            if (str[str.length - 2] == 'X' && str[str.length - 1] == 'X') {\n                if (ending.equals(\"00\")) {\n                    xDigit = '0';\n                } else {\n                    return; // invalid for other endings\n                }\n            } else if (str[str.length - 2] == 'X') {\n                xDigit = firstEnd;\n            } else {\n                xDigit = secondEnd;\n            }\n        }\n\n        // Check for leading zero constraint\n        if (str[0] == '0') return; // original string starts with 0, invalid\n        if (str[0] == 'X' && xDigit != 'n' && xDigit == '0') return; // X at start would be 0\n        if (str[0] == '_' && xDigit == '0') {\n            // If X is constrained to 0 and first char is _, we need to be careful\n            // But _ can be any digit, so we'll handle in counting\n        }\n\n        long count = 1;\n        boolean xUsed = (xDigit != 'n');\n\n        // Process each position except last two\n        for (int i = 0; i < str.length - 2; i++) {\n            if (str[i] == '_') {\n                if (i == 0) {\n                    count *= 9; // can't be 0\n                } else {\n                    count *= 10;\n                }\n            } else if (str[i] == 'X') {\n                if (i == 0) {\n                    count *= 9; // can't be 0\n                } else {\n                    count *= 10;\n                }\n            }\n        }\n\n        // Check if X constraint affects leading zero\n        if (str[0] == 'X' && xDigit == '0') {\n            // X at start would be 0, invalid\n            return;\n        }\n\n        // Special case: if the entire number would be 0\n        boolean allZero = true;\n        for (int i = 0; i < str.length; i++) {\n            if (str[i] != '0' && str[i] != '_' && str[i] != 'X') {\n                allZero = false;\n                break;\n            }\n            if (str[i] == 'X' && xDigit != '0') {\n                allZero = false;\n                break;\n            }\n        }\n\n        if (allZero && str.length > 1) {\n            // \"00\" or \"000\" etc. is actually 0, which is divisible by 25\n            // But leading zeros make it invalid except for single 0\n            // However, problem says 0000 has three leading zeroes, so it's invalid\n            // Only single \"0\" is valid\n            if (str.length == 1) {\n                result += 1;\n            }\n            return;\n        }\n\n        result += count;\n    }\n}\n</repaired_code>\n<confidence>\n0.3\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-8.344646857949556e-07, -4.410646579344757e-05, -4.291525328881107e-06, -1.0728830375228426e-06, -0.00048458753735758364, -4.3748852476710454e-05, -0.0004306104383431375, -0.0005909841856919229, -4.529942543740617e-06, -6.651657167822123e-05, -3.576278118089249e-07, -0.0005075835506431758, -5.602820692729438e-06, -3.576278118089249e-07, -2.312633478140924e-05, -0.12693707644939423, -0.42871594429016113, -0.0008198237628675997, -1.4305104514278355e-06, -0.07717707008123398, -1.0728830375228426e-06, -0.006728373933583498, -0.03804221749305725, -1.6927575416048057e-05, -7.271740287251305e-06, -4.887569048150908e-06, -0.06225799769163132, -0.0002302858338225633, -0.021205605939030647, -0.0005476167425513268, -0.07889217138290405, 0.0, -3.6954811548639555e-06, -2.3841855067985307e-07, 0.0, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -5.125986263010418e-06, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -1.0728830375228426e-06, -4.887569048150908e-06, -8.344646857949556e-07, -8.344646857949556e-07, -3.576278118089249e-07, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -1.7881233361549675e-05, -7.152555099310121e-07, -0.00017677174764685333, -5.07818695041351e-05, -2.50339189733495e-06, -4.0531076592742465e-06, -3.099393507000059e-05, -0.3678959012031555, -0.1404893547296524, -1.1205610462639015e-05, -1.1920922133867862e-06, -1.0728830375228426e-06, -5.960462772236497e-07, -1.311301275563892e-06, -8.344646857949556e-07, -0.00020668754586949944, -8.4638240878121e-06, -7.986990567587782e-06, -2.074220174108632e-05, -2.6225699912174605e-05, -0.0011337526375427842, -1.1920922133867862e-06, -1.0013530300057027e-05, -1.5497195136049413e-06, 0.0, -3.576278118089249e-07, -3.814689989667386e-06, -1.549708758830093e-05, -1.0251946150674485e-05, -2.9802276912960224e-06, -6.794906312279636e-06, -0.0003389737685211003, -0.0024781490210443735, -0.005967182572931051, 0.0, -1.2993727978027891e-05, -1.19209